## A Structured To-Do List

Each task has a title, priority level, and completion status. An enum for priority keeps labels consistent.

### The Priority Enum

```xiom
enum Priority {
  Low,
  Medium,
  High,
  Urgent,
}
```

### The Task Struct

```xiom
type Task = {
  title: Str;
  priority: Priority;
  done: Bool;
}
```

### Creating Tasks

```xiom
let fix_bug = Task{
  title: "Fix login crash";
  priority: Priority.Urgent;
  done: false;
};

let water_plants = Task{
  title: "Water the plants";
  priority: Priority.Low;
  done: true;
};
```

### Describing a Task

A function that turns a task into a human-readable string by checking its priority and status:

```xiom
fn describe(t: Task) -> Str {
  let status = "INCOMPLETE";
  if t.done {
    status = "DONE";
  }
  let label = "[LOW]";
  if t.priority == Priority.Medium { label = "[MEDIUM]"; }
  if t.priority == Priority.High { label = "[HIGH]"; }
  if t.priority == Priority.Urgent { label = "[URGENT]"; }
  return label + " " + t.title + " — " + status;
}
```

Using it:

```xiom
describe(fix_bug);       // "[URGENT] Fix login crash — INCOMPLETE"
describe(water_plants);  // "[LOW] Water the plants — DONE"
```

